  "actor_type": "state-associated",
  "affiliation": [
    "PLA"
  ],
  "affiliation_unit": "Unit 61486",
  "affiliation_detail": "Associated by Crowdstrike (2014) to 12th Bureau of the PLA's 3rd General Staff Department (GSD), Unit 61486, which is believed to be headquartered in the Zhabei District of Shanghai, China. The 12th Bureau supports China's space surveillance network and is suspected to be involved in space-based SIGINT collection and interception of satellite communications.\nCrowdStrike identified Chen Ping (alias \"cpyy\") as an individual responsible for domain registration of Putter Panda C2 infrastructure.\n",
  "affiliation_confidence": "likely",
  "entity_name": null,
  "last_seen": "2016",
  "first_seen": "2007",
  "first_described": "2014-06",
  "description": "APT2, tracked by CrowdStrike as Putter Panda, is a Chinese state-sponsored cyber espionage group attributed to PLA Unit 61486, the 12th Bureau of the 3rd General Staff Department, headquartered in Shanghai's Zhabei District. \nActive since at least 2007, the group primarily targeted the U.S. defense industry and European satellite,  aerospace, and communications sectors, consistent with the 12th Bureau's mission of space surveillance and satellite SIGINT collection.\nAPT2 relied on spear-phishing emails exploiting vulnerabilities in Adobe Reader and Microsoft Office to deploy custom remote access tools.  The group notably targeted conference attendees, particularly golf players, leading to its \"Putter Panda\" codename. \nCrowdStrike's 2014 report identified shared infrastructure with PLA Unit 61398 (APT1/Comment Panda),  suggesting coordination between PLA cyber units. \nA 2016 Cylance report found the group had retooled with new backdoors achieving zero antivirus detection after its public exposure.\n",
  "attack_group_id": "G0024",
  "attack_group_url": "https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0024/",
